    "description": "``DOMChildNode`` is an interface introduced in version 8.0 for DOM nodes that can have siblings. It is implemented by ``DOMElement``, ``DOMText``, ``DOMComment``, ``DOMProcessingInstruction``, and ``DOMDocumentType``.\n\nIt provides ``before()`` and ``after()`` to insert nodes adjacent to the current node, ``replaceWith()`` to replace it, and ``remove()`` to detach it from its parent.",
    "code": "<?php\n\n    $dom = new DOMDocument;\n    $dom->loadHTML('<p>Hello <b>world</b></p>');\n    $b = $dom->getElementsByTagName('b')->item(0);\n    $b->remove();\n\n?>",
